# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, one module).
#
# docker/Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so this file is what keeps that cheap: it drops everything the
# build does not need, and it stops a stale target/ shadowing what the builder stage compiles.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and hundreds of MB of it here
# (target/ carries the native sources dir and the compiled binary).
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.settings
.factorypath
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docs
docker
